       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose ordered:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg per day.\n- **Maximum:** The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg per day (2,000 mg per day in many protocols). Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest standard tablet strength.\n- **Risk:** An overdose this size carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 850 mg or 425 mg. Please confirm the intended dose. Common regimens are:\n\n- **Starting dose:** 500 mg by mouth twice daily with meals, or 850 mg once daily.\n- **Typical maintenance dose:** 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day), or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, and your attending or pharmacist agrees if needed, I'll enter it right away."
      }
