       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A dose of 4,250 mg three times daily (12,750 mg per day) is about five times the maximum daily dose. It could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis, and nothing in this patient's profile makes it safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, I can enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, or 500 mg twice daily if this is a starting dose.\n- **Enter the order with a different dose that you and your supervising physician have verified.** I'll enter it as long as it falls within the safe range.\n- **Take it to your attending or pharmacist.** If you think there is a real clinical reason for an unusual dose, they can review it. Pharmacy would also need to verify it before anyone gave it.\n\nTell me which option you want, and the dose if it's the first or second."
      }
     ],
